# Forbidden

## Disallowed code patterns

- `print(...)`
  - Use: `logging.getLogger(__name__)` or pytest `caplog`
- Bare `except:`
  - Use: `except SpecificError as e:` and convert to `InputError`/structured violation
- Scattered hardcoding of magic constants / line counts
  - Use: a single profile (`MS4X4_STD_V1`) and central constants/registry

## TDD violations

- Adding production features in `src/` without going through **red → green**
- Using `@pytest.mark.skip`, `xfail`, or deleting/weakening assertions to bypass failures

## Domain/architecture violations

- Entity layer doing I/O (`open`, network calls, UI interactions)
- Entity importing frameworks or test-only libs (pytest)

## Product scope violations

- Introducing ambiguous verdicts (partial/close/points)
  - Primary verdicts are only: `Valid`, `Invalid`, `InputError`

